<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muslim conquest of the Levant and Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">637–642 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Arab conquest of Egypt and Syria · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/early-muslim-conquests">Early Muslim conquests</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Muslim conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/levant">Levant</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> refers to the Arab campaigns that took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> and Egypt from Byzantine control in the seventh century. The site's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> profile dates the loss of Egypt and Syria to 637–642 CE and describes it as the empire's most economically devastating event, eliminating roughly 40 percent of imperial tax revenue and permanently truncating the Byzantine commercial system.</p></div>
